{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-hotelling-sourcetypes-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-hotelling-sourcetypes`, `rates-hotelling` with the diesel combination SHORT-haul truck (61) and single-unit short-haul truck (52) selected beside the long-haul truck (62) -- the same processes (17, 90, 91 and its retag 93), Washtenaw County, road types 1 and 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. Whether MOVES writes a hotelling RATE for a source type with no hotelling hours. At Rates scale RatePerHour is a rate and not a quotient (shore power has one where its hours are zero), so a rate could exist without activity. It does not: MOVES writes the same 491 rows as `rates-hotelling`, every one source type 62's, because BaseRateGenerator's steps 200 and 210 write RatesOpModeDistribution rows for 62 alone -- `cohMode_hotellingWeight` is 0 off it. Closes PLAN.md §7.3.48's last hotelling item.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1, `n_outputRate` the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`, and the source-bin and physics-row counts of three source types.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-hotelling"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
